<% @title = "Privacy — Amber Framework" %>
<% @meta = "Amber Framework does not use analytics, advertising trackers, cookies, forms, or third-party runtime assets on this website." %>

<header class="page-hero privacy-hero">
  <div class="site-container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Short on purpose</p>
    <h1>We do not track you.</h1>
    <p>This website is documentation, not a surveillance system.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<main class="section">
  <div class="content-narrow policy-copy">
    <div class="privacy-summary">
      <strong>No analytics.</strong><strong>No advertising.</strong><strong>No cookies.</strong><strong>No forms.</strong><strong>No third-party runtime assets.</strong>
    </div>

    <h2>What the site collects</h2>
    <p>The Amber Framework website does not intentionally collect personal information from visitors. It does not load Google Analytics, Google Tag Manager, tracking pixels, hosted font APIs, advertising scripts, or behavioral analytics.</p>

    <h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
    <p>The site does not set cookies and does not use local storage or session storage. Interactive examples run in the page and do not persist visitor activity.</p>

    <h2>Locally served assets</h2>
    <p>Essential stylesheets, JavaScript, fonts, and images are served from the same Amber Framework site. Links to GitHub, Discord, Crystal, or another website leave this privacy boundary only after you choose them.</p>

    <h2>Infrastructure logs</h2>
    <p>Like most web hosting infrastructure, the host may process ordinary request information needed to deliver and secure the service, such as an IP address, requested path, timestamp, and user agent. The Amber website does not use those logs to build visitor profiles or for advertising.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If the project adds analytics, accounts, forms, or another data-collecting feature, this policy will be updated before that feature is enabled.</p>

    <p class="policy-date">Last updated August 10, 2026.</p>
  </div>
</main>
